    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d31">

                <pb facs="0054" n="42" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg42"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851T.01/12⁴⁄₆</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by Mr. Perry N. Jester of the Division of
                        Near Eastern Affairs</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-12-28">December 28, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Reference is made to previous memoranda on the subject of recommending the
                    appointment of a personal representative of the President with the rank of
                    ambassador or minister to work with Lord Swinton at Accra, and to represent the
                    interests of this Government and nation near the governments of the United
                    Nations’ territories in Africa.</p>
                <pb facs="0055" n="43" xml:id="pg43"/>
                <p>Following the return of the file on the subject mentioned just above from the
                    Secretary’s Office with the directive that we reconsider the matter with a view
                    to recommending an appointment of medium rank (interpreted to mean that the
                    appointment of a personal representative of the President to the territories
                    named was not desired). Mr. Villard stated that in his opinion it would not now
                    be necessary to refer this matter to the War Department for their concurrence or
                    approval; that with regard to the appointment of a Commissioner or other State
                    Department representative, this Department could make and carry out a unilateral
                    decision.</p>
                <p>[Here follow suggestions as to the choice of a Commissioner and an
                    assistant.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Perry N. Jester</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
